  "id": "general-health-questionnaire",
  "term": "General Health Questionnaire",
  "definition": "The General Health Questionnaire, especially its 12-item form, is a brief screening measure used to assess psychological distress, detect mental health difficulties, and track short-term changes in mental well-being. It is widely used across different populations and settings, though score interpretation may vary between groups.",
